Summary: EnableMouseInPointer semi-stub: turn it on and send WM_POINTER messages for mouse input
Category: input
Kind: fix
Origin: winehq
  Version: 11.4
  Commit: 71b686ce9fdce65416080c834a9103a743dc095c,
    b94237cd34864bd8f920b44532f7827a73784563
  Bugs: 59415
  MR: 10120
  Authors: Rémi Bernon, Paul Gofman
  URL: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/71b686ce9fdce65416080c834a9103a743dc095c,
    https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/b94237cd34864bd8f920b44532f7827a73784563
  Changes: win32u_private.h context differs (10.0 has destroy_caret there);
    the user32 test hunks that drop todo_wine from pointer message sequences
    are left out, as 10.0's test_GetPointerInfo has no such checks
  Note: 71b686ce9fdc is in Wine 11.3 (committed 2026-02-19), b94237cd3486
    in 11.4. Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships the first: its win32u has the
    semi-stub and the mouse-to-WM_POINTER conversion.
Upstream: yes (Wine 11.3; the button fix, b94237cd3486, since Wine 11.4)
Needed until: 11.4 (WineHQ b94237cd3486)
Why: EnableMouseInPointer and IsMouseInPointerEnabled were stubs that
 failed. Now the first EnableMouseInPointer call sets the process-wide
 state, a later call asking for the opposite fails with
 ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED, and while it is enabled each mouse move, button and
 wheel message also sends the window the matching WM_POINTER* message
 (except for mouse input generated from pen or touch). WM_POINTERDOWN comes
 only for the first button pressed and WM_POINTERUP only when the last is
 released, as on Windows (b94237cd; without it a second button sent a
 second WM_POINTERDOWN and two WM_POINTERUPs).
Programs: In Falsus demo (Unreal Engine, WineHQ bug 59415): no input after
 the title screen. Unity 6 games (bug 53847: The Planet Crafter, How to
 Fish): the mouse is ignored
Uncertain: whether it's enough for every Unity 6 game: WineHQ bug 53847 is
 still open, and so is bug 59429 (In Falsus's rhythm sections, after this
 fix).
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-25: build0 (without b94237cd) passes mouse-in-pointer
 (i686, x86_64); a probe there got a second WM_POINTERDOWN and two
 WM_POINTERUPs with two buttons.
 10.0: 2026-11-26: WineHQ b94237cd (pointer button flags) added, applies as
 is
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

